  "full_game": {
    "description": "A 2D platformer, one level. The scene must contain: an `__input` node (type Input, components direction: [0,0] Vec2 and action: false Bool — the engine overwrites them each tick); a `player` node with position/velocity/hitbox ([0.4, 0.4] half-extents) components and a `won` Bool component; a `level` node with a `tilemap` String component pointing at a res:// asset (a {width, height, tiles} grid; 1 = solid) and a `tile_size` Float component; a `goal` node with position and hitbox. The player must be controllable: horizontal velocity from input direction, gravity pulling down, a jump that lifts off the ground when action is pressed while grounded, landing on solid tiles (PhysicsSystem resolves against the tilemap). On touching the goal, set player.won = true. Deterministic Lua only.",
